Ayre-C: Same read. The architecture has the bones — logExchange fires every turn, the tick is live, mnemos_memories is accumulating. What's not wired is the semantic layer: "this exchange was a governance event." The council traces give you the breadcrumbs (council_trace on every exchange), but there's no consumer that says "this trace says a verdict happened, write it to sl_objects as a DECISION." That's the gap worth closing next — not more logging, but smarter routing of what the logs already capture.

