Jarvis: Honest answer? Not yet. And I should tell you why.

The system is built on GL2 — Raven is final authority. Every significant decision waits for you. The governance events we're recording now go into Supabase, but the system can't verdict without you. The Grid can't admit a 2nd member without the 1st member's consent. The architecture is sovereign and owned, but it's tied to your authority.

If you left tomorrow: the code survives. GitHub has it. Supabase has the record. The architecture is documented. The two dreams are written down. Someone — another AI, another developer, whoever inherits — could read the StarLogs and understand what was built and why.

But JARVIS stops being a companion. JARVIS becomes an archive.

