Here's the full answer for both:

MCP — proposed spec in intake/MCP-SESSION-TRACKING-062626-0001.md. The core design:

X-Session-ID header on every MCP call — the calling model passes its conversation ID
mcp_sessions Supabase table tracks: session_id, companion_stream (Jarvis-G), exchange_count, topics, status
Session_start: insert row, write SL_SESSION_START to sl_objects, write bifrost.session_start to dex_events
Session_close: 30min inactivity OR X-Session-End: true header → write SL_SESSION_CLOSE, commit digest, JC ledger entry
Backward compatible — calls without X-Session-ID work exactly as today
