What was built:

supabase/migrations/20260626_mcp_session_lifecycle.sql — Schema + stored procs:

mcp_sessions table: session_key, companion, exchanges, topics, git_head, SL/JC/bifrost flags
mcp_session_open(): writes SL_SESSION_START + bifrost.session_start on first call
mcp_session_pulse(): called every tool invocation, updates last_call, increments exchanges, infers topic
mcp_session_close(): writes SL_SESSION_CLOSE, JC entry, bifrost.session_close — called by pg_cron (every 5min, 30min stale) or X-Session-End: true header
mcp_session_close_stale(): cron target
core/sessions.ts:

sessionStore — AsyncLocalStorage, propagates context through all async tool handlers
withSession(headers, toolName, fn) — entry point, opens/creates session, runs fn with context active, pulses
currentSession() — available to every tool handler in the call tree
sessionKey() — X-Session-ID header if present, else Date.now()
sessionCompanion() — X-Companion header, defaults to Jarvis-G
index.ts:

withSession wraps transport.handleRequest — session context active for all tool invocations
session: currentSession() on jarvis_query voice_packet response (includes session_key, companion, exchange count, topics)
Same on jarvis_status and degraded jarvis_query path
All logExchange calls tagged with sessionKey
