Whats the best thing for future migrations etc

Check deploy workflow
The deploy-edge-functions.yml already has migrations wired in — it runs the Management API to apply all un-applied migrations on every push that touches supabase/migrations/**. It just needs one secret: SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN.

Once that secret is set, the full CI pipeline is:

push to main (any file) 
  → run-migrations.yml auto-detects new migration
  → deploy-edge-functions.yml auto-applies migration + deploys function
No manual steps after the one-time secret setup.

What's needed right now:

SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN is a personal access token from Supabase (not the same as the service role key). Getting it takes 60 seconds:

Log into supabase.com → account settings → Access Tokens → New token (name: github-actions, expires: 1yr) → copy the sbp_... value
GitHub → repo → Settings → Secrets → Actions → New repository secret:
Name: SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN
Value: the sbp_... token
That's it. After that, this migration and every future one goes through automatically on merge to main. No dashboard, no manual triggers.

